# macOS
.DS_Store

# build artifacts
*.o
# stub .so files are generated from stub/*.c by the Makefile
stub/*.so
# cross-compiled binary + packaging output
pkg/plxnative
pkg/threadprobe
pkg/*.ipk
pkg/ipk.sha256

# ipk packaging staging (regenerated by `make ipk`)
ipkroot/*.tar.gz
ipkroot/debian-binary
ipkroot/data/usr/

# reference copies of the TV's proprietary shared libs — not needed to build
# (the build links against the stub .so files generated from stub/*.c)
sysroot/

# local dev overrides (real PMS host + X-Plex-Token)
local.env
src/config.local.h
# ...and every agent worktree carries its OWN copy of that file, with the real token in it.
# These were held out of the index by .git/info/exclude, which is local-only: it does not survive
# a clone, is not reviewable, and does not apply in a fresh worktree or a CI checkout. On a repo
# about to go public that is the difference between "ignored" and "one `git add -A` from a live
# credential in history". Belongs here, in the tracked file, where anyone can see it.
.claude/worktrees/
# the on-device suite's installation-specific half: which PMS, which TV, which ratingKeys, which
# Plex Home user. tests/manifest.json keeps the case DEFINITIONS (public); this keeps the private
# library inventory that used to be committed alongside them. See tests/manifest.local.json.example.
tests/manifest.local.json
rust-modules/target/
rust-modules/target-release/
rust-modules/target-sim/
rust-modules/target-macapp/
# `make LAB=1` and `make LAB=1 sim` — the Lab Diagnostics feature set gets its own build trees for
# the reason every other feature set does (cargo does not hash its output; see the Makefile).
rust-modules/target-lab/
rust-modules/target-sim-lab/

# dead prototype dir (code lives in rust-modules/ now)
rust-poc/
.abi-cache/
.tv-mac
# which television this working copy talks to (Makefile TV, tools/ TV_HOST) — one line, an IP or
# hostname. Local because it is the maintainer's home network, not a project fact.
.tv-host
.tv-stream.pid
.tv-stream.log
pkg/sockprobe
pkg/logmprobe

# tv-session.sh --remote: the published URL, the generated password and the tunnel/front-end
# scratch. NEVER commit a password, and never commit a URL that is live while it is live.
.tv-dpad.pid
.tv-dpad.log
.tv-dpad-pass
.tv-tunnel.pid
.tv-tunnel.log
.tv-remote-url
pkg/.build-config
# The derived per-flavour descriptor (ci/mkipk.py --emit-appinfo). Generated from the tracked
# pkg/appinfo.json by ci/flavor.py on every deploy/package, so committing it would put the version
# in a fifth file. NB `pkg/dev/` is the opposite — tracked artwork, cut by tools/mkicons.py.
pkg/.flavor/

# Bundled FFmpeg: the upstream source tree and the build output. Both are DERIVED —
# ci/build-ffmpeg.sh reproduces them from a sha256-pinned tarball — and the tree alone is
# 30k files. The .ipk carries the four built .so; releases carry the tarball for LGPL.
# **No trailing slash on these two, deliberately.** A pattern ending in `/` matches a DIRECTORY
# and nothing else — so a worktree that reaches the shared build by SYMLINKING
# `vendor/ffmpeg-prefix` at the main checkout (the cheap way to avoid a 2-minute, 280 MB rebuild
# per agent) was NOT ignored, and one `git add -A` staged the link. What that commits is a
# machine-specific absolute path that resolves to nothing on anyone else's disk, in a file nobody
# reads twice. Slashless, both a real directory and a link to one are ignored.
vendor/ffmpeg-build
vendor/ffmpeg-prefix
vendor/sentry-native-*.tar.gz
vendor/sentry-native-src
vendor/sentry-native-build
vendor/sentry-native-prefix
# A NESTED vendor/, which is not a thing anyone writes on purpose — it is what
# `cp -R <repo>/vendor <worktree>/vendor` produces when the destination already exists,
# and seeding parallel worktrees that way put 30,247 build-artefact files (280 MB, plus
# the upstream builder's MAC addresses and home path in FFmpeg's configure logs) into a
# branch bound for a PUBLIC repository. Caught in the pre-push scan; ignored here so the
# next person seeding a fleet cannot repeat it.
vendor/vendor/
# ...and the copies staged into pkg/ for the package. Equally derived: pkg/plxnative depends on
# them, so a fresh clone rebuilds FFmpeg either way, and tracking them costs 2.1 MB per version
# bump forever in a repo whose reproducibility rests on the pinned tarball.
pkg/lib*-plx.so.*
pkg/.ffabi-ok

# Session file the app writes next to its payload. The desktop simulator is pointed at
# pkg/ via PLXNATIVE_APP_DIR, so it lands here on a host run; it can hold plex.tv and PMS
# tokens, and this repository is public.
pkg/auth.json

# The Lab Diagnostics session file (docs/lab-diagnostics.md), written by `tools/plxnative-lab
# start` and staged into a `make LAB=1` package. It holds a live bearer secret and the developer's
# own endpoint; `ci/check-package.py` refuses any non-LAB package that contains it.
pkg/lab.json

# `make macapp` output: the macOS application bundle, its zip, and the recipient's README copy.
# Build products, like pkg/plxnative and the .ipk above — and the bundle carries ~10 copied
# Homebrew dylibs, which are neither ours to commit nor meaningful outside the machine that
# assembled them. ci/mkmacapp.py rebuilds all three in about a minute.
pkg/PlxNative.app/
pkg/PlxNative-*.zip
pkg/PlxNative-README.md

# Generated test media (tests/fixtures/make_fixtures.py, `make fixtures`). The default output
# root is ~/plxnative-fixtures and the generator REFUSES an --out anywhere inside this repo, so
# these patterns should never match anything — they are here for the case where somebody points
# a build at the tree by hand or the guard is ever weakened. Media is ~2.5 GB per set and is
# reproducible from the script, so none of it belongs in a public repository's history.
tests/fixtures/out/
tests/fixtures/**/*.mkv
tests/fixtures/**/*.mp4
tests/fixtures/**/*.sup
tests/fixtures/fixtures.json

# Python bytecode from the host-side test/tooling scripts.
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# The HOST FFmpeg the desktop simulator streams through (ci/build-ffmpeg.sh HOST=1) — derived,
# ~2 MB of Mach-O, and never shipped: APP_FILES is an explicit list, so it cannot reach an .ipk.
#
# SLASHLESS, for exactly the reason spelled out above `vendor/ffmpeg-prefix` — a fleet lane
# SYMLINKS these at another checkout's prebuilt trees so it does not rebuild FFmpeg, and a trailing
# slash matches a directory and NOT a link to one. So the trailing-slash form ignored the real
# directory and let the symlink through: one `git add -A` on 2026-09-02 committed a machine-local
# absolute path that resolves to nothing on anyone else's disk, and a later one re-committed it
# after it had been removed. Both forms are covered without the slash.
vendor/ffmpeg-build-host
vendor/ffmpeg-prefix-host
pkg/*.dylib
pkg/.ffabi-host-ok
rust-modules/target-sym/
rust-modules/target-release-sym/
pkg/plxnative.debug
pkg/telemetry.local.json
